h diplomatic  relations 69% of New Democrats and 63%  of Bloc Quebecois voters also agree with  that idea but just 47 percent of  conservative voters believe it is time  to re-establish formal ties with Iran  for now though the government of  candidates priorities are to move  forward with the investigation as to the  future of Canada Iran relations Canadian  officials say that's a discussion for  another day Robin David akin in Ottawa  some terrifying moments at an airport in  Istanbul a passenger plane broke into  several pieces and burst into flames  after it skidded off the runway and  crashed into a field emergency personnel  swarmed the Boeing 737 to rescue  passengers many of whom had to escape  through cracks in the smashed plane it  belonged to low-cost carrier Pegasus  Airlines the plane was arriving from a  Western Province in Turkey and was  carrying a hundred and seventy-one  passengers and six crew members there  was heavy rain and strong winds at the  time of the crash  in eastern Turkey emergency crews  desperately tried to dig survivors out  of deep snow an avalanche slammed into a  mountain road wiping out a huge team of  rescue workers sent to find people  missing in an earlier snow slide at  least 38 people were killed in the two  avalanches dozens more were injured a  fossilized skeleton belonging to an  ancient iguana like creature that roamed  the ocean more than 200 million years  ago  has been discovered preserved in rock in  southeastern Alaska the species of  marine reptile is called the lattice or  meaning ocean lizard and it's a distant  cousin of the dinosaurs that lived  during the Triassic period they have  been found in the past but this one is  different it has a needle-like snout and  as the only intact the lattice or fossil  ever found in North America zero gravity  mega record affects the astronaut who  broke the highest glass ceiling three  astronauts are heading home tonight  including Christina cook she spent three  hundred and twenty eight days on the  International Space Station breaking the  record for the longest stint in space by  a woman and as Eric Sorenson explains  it's not the only record she was a part  of as women catch up to the achievements  of men the bell signals today's command  hand over to a new crew aboard the  International Space Station it caps a  phenomenal flight for American Christina  cook cooks 11 months in space was only  12 days short of the all-time record for  a single mission Christina relocates the  apsr cook and fellow astronaut Jessica  Muir also blazed a trail when they  worked outside the spacecraft together  the first ever all-female spacewalk she  and I both really appreciated and loved  that it could serve as inspiration for  future space explorers  the very first woman in space was  valentina Tereshkova of the Soviet Union  in 1963 she followed eleven men into  space everyone wants to be an abaya  and was a hero in the soviet union even  if the description sounds out-of-date he  it seemed to be Tereshkova was the first  and for a long time the only woman in  space the very first space traveler was  Soviet cosmonaut Yuri Gagarin in April  1961 over the next 20 years to April  1981 there were 103 astronauts mostly  Soviet and American men and there was  Tereshkova one woman representing less  than 1% of all astronauts today after  almost 60 years of spaceflight  there have been 564 astronauts in total  women now account for 65 of them or just  over 11% it's progress  Canada did its part to breakthrough the  atmospheric glass ceiling our first  astronaut was Marc Garneau but the  second was Roberta Bondar  she and later Julie Payette performed  every bit as well as the men who had  gone before and while women haven't  caught up in sheer numbers they have  closed the gap as more embrace science  and technology as that pipeline of women  in STEM and other underrepresented folks  in the STEM fields grows we hope to then  capitalize on that and bring that  innovation and talent into the astronaut  corps and someday perhaps the  breakthroughs will come not just for  being the first woman but simply being  the first period  Eric Sorenson Global News Toronto well  said that is global national for this  Wednesday I'm Robin Gill tonight your  Canada is Richmond BC we would love to  see you're part of this country so email  us your pictures thank you for watching  and have a great night  [Music]
 

